# Keep the Docker build context small. Everything in here is excluded
# before the build daemon sees the repo. Without this, the root
# node_modules alone is ~1.7 GB and every Railway build re-uploads it.

# Dependencies (re-installed inside the image)
**/node_modules

# Build output
**/dist
**/.next
**/.next-smoke
**/.turbo
**/build
**/out
**/.output

# pnpm
.pnpm-store

# Test + smoke artifacts
test-results
playwright-report
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output

# Local-only runtime state
backups
.airjam
**/.cache

# Editor / OS
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*

# Local env (the Dockerfile reads build args, not files)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env.local

# Docs / dev-only repo files that aren't needed inside the image.
# (Keep `content/` and `docs/` — the platform build reads them.)
*.md
!README.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
